			<div class="content" id="post-content-1865680">
									

<p>The tone needs work. The afforementioned &quot;hellish&quot; is an example. But i hit a harder roadblock at the second line of the containment proceedures. The tone there just feels&#8230;. really rough. It's too casual. The containment proceedures themselves should be expanded as well. This thing activated based on people seeing it, right? So wouldn;t it be better to keep in in some kind of individual container, rather than a file cabinet? We don;t want people activating it by accident.</p>
<p>It might be smart to vague up the &quot;compulsion&quot; a bit. Rather than flat out state it, why not have it simply be an observation, and not directly connected to the artifact. Or better yet, if the competitiveness increased as items were collected. That way, they might fairly innocently collect the benign items, just for the hell of it, but increasingly want to win and be more willing to do the damaging activities. Just a thought bouncing in my head.</p>
<p>I'll give this a tentative +1, based on the potential and the fact that you're responding so well to feedback.</p>

